Define additional actions where necessary, but do not leave existing app buttons connected only to local simulation.

For control changes, validate each command and its permitted state transition.

The start, pause, resume, dry-run and retry controls must cause real backend changes. A successful API response must not falsely claim that an automation job has completed when it has only been queued.

Return an explicit state such as "DISPATCHED", "QUEUED", "RUNNING", "PAUSED", "COMPLETED", "FAILED" or "UNKNOWN" as appropriate.

3.3 Required engine actions

